 <div class="txt"><p class="eyebrow">What is Ayni</p><h2 class="h2">Ayni is the Andean way of sacred reciprocity: <em>when you give, you receive.</em></h2>
  <p>Once a year we live it out loud. We learned Ayni from the families we work with in Peru: one multigenerational family farm we work with directly, in the Sacred Valley region just outside Cusco, in the ceja de selva, the eyebrow of the jungle. They work hand in hand with the Quechua and Machiguenga farming families around them, care for old cacao trees the way their families always have, and make the paste and wrap every bar at the farm.</p>
  <p>We pay them 3x above fair trade and buy direct, with no broker in between. It&rsquo;s not transactional. It&rsquo;s relational. This week is our way of passing that on.</p>
  <p>Every batch is tested for heavy metals, herbicides and pesticides. <a href="/pages/safe-cacao" style="color:var(--head);">See the lab results.</a></p>
